name: "SOC-UC-005-Linux-Crontab Modification for Persistence"

description: |
  Detects modifications to crontab files or execution of the crontab
  command on Linux systems by non-root users or unexpected processes.
  Attackers abuse cron to establish persistence by scheduling malicious
  commands to execute at regular intervals, surviving reboots and
  maintaining long-term access without requiring active sessions.
  This technique is associated with MITRE ATT&CK T1053.003
  (Scheduled Task/Job: Cron) and is commonly observed in the
  persistence phase following initial compromise.

author:
  - "HRISHIKESH YALAVARTHI"

enabled: true
type: esql
language: esql

severity: "high"
risk_score: 73

